index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..cec6ccacb9885b52d9b8428b221c3bf85e4bbe50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/02-independent-classification.log
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+INDEPENDENT CLASSIFICATION RESULT
+
+Entries 1-2 are DEFINITION: isNumericVal and orderablePair name total proof-domain predicates.
+Entries 3-6 are DEFINITION: the guarded, structurally descending scanDefined recurrence.
+Entries 7-17 are DEFINITION: the ten disjoint orderable orderGe equations plus its guarded non-orderable totalization.
+Entries 18-22 are DEFINITION: the guarded, structurally descending arrangeSeq recurrence and totalization.
+Entry 23 is DOMAIN_LEMMA: it equates the pre-existing operational observation applyCmp(">=",V,W) with the new summary orderGe under orderablePair. It does not define either left-hand symbol. It is directly relevant because the source loop executes >= and scanDefined admits numeric pairs and string pairs.
+
+No entry is an OPERATIONAL_RULE. No entry is a PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA. The ten claims in connection-spec.k are sort-specialized and are not the exact dynamic guarded rule at verification.k:106-108. Every simplification rule is classified as DEFINITION or DOMAIN_LEMMA.
+
+Case audit of the domain lemma against frozen operational semantics:
+- Int/Int: int.k applyCmp >= is >=Int; orderGe is >=Int.
+- Bool/Bool, Bool/Int, Int/Bool: bool.k promotes through boolAsInt; orderGe does the same.
+- Float/Float: float.k applyCmp >= is notBool floatLt; orderGe is identical.
+- Int/Float and Float/Int: float.k uses notBool ltIF / notBool ltFI; orderGe is identical.
+- Bool/Float and Float/Bool: float.k first applies boolAsInt and then the same mixed rule; orderGe is identical.
+- Str/Str: str.k applyCmp >= is notBool strLt; orderGe is identical.
+
+COMMAND
+kprove connection-spec.k --definition connection-kompiled --spec-module CONNECTION-SPEC
+(cwd /reference/k-proof)
+
+RESULT (exit 0; warning bodies abridged only here, full salient result retained)
+Ten WarnTrivialClaim warnings, one for each claims at lines 7, 10, 13, 16, 19, 22, 25, 28, 31, and 34-37.
+#Top
+The compiled main module is VERIFICATION-BASE, so the dynamic rule in VERIFICATION is not imported. These ten specialized claims still do not satisfy the exact-rule requirement for PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA.
+
