diff --git a/evidence/09-operational-adversarial.log b/evidence/09-operational-adversarial.log
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..54a26e820c4494b091229fbb7686b466df462da0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/evidence/09-operational-adversarial.log
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+AUDIT FILE
+AuditOperational.lean imports Proof, constructs Int/Bool/Float SortVal
+witnesses, evaluates the candidate applyCmp binding on boundary cases, proves
+SortStr is empty, and proves the fixed target for a deliberately false
+counterfactual parameter interpretation.
+
+COMMAND
+env LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/proc-self-readlink-shim.so lake env lean AuditOperational.lean
+
+RESULT (exit 0; exact output)
+("int 2 >= 1", true)
+("int -1 >= 0", false)
+("true >= 1", true)
+("0 >= true", false)
+("2^53+1 >= 2^53-float", true)
+("2^53-float >= 2^53+1", false)
+("positive infinity >= 0", true)
+("negative infinity >= 0", false)
+("NaN >= 0 under supplied K not(<) rule", true)
+("minimum positive subnormal >= 0", true)
+("non-orderable noneV is totalized to false by candidate", false)
+
+JUDGMENT
+The reachable numeric cases agree with the frozen K rules, including the
+supplied semantics' deliberate `notBool floatLt` behavior on NaN. The
+non-orderable false result is outside the domain-lemma guard. No string test can
+be constructed because the generated SortStr is empty; this is the decisive
+bridge failure. The counterfactual false functions also prove the target,
+confirming that the equation does not itself validate the parameter meanings.
+
